      "CAROLINE: O.K. .\nROSE: I thought you needed help in the kitchen? ;\nCAROLINE: Well, everything's in the dining room. Why don't you light the candles, that would be good?\nROSE: Bitch.",
      "CAROLINE: We are having a Scandinavian family Christmas roast with fresh baked Kringlors, seven day old traditional Lutfish and Lamb Gookins.\nCAROLINE: I'm sure you all must be wondering about my outfit and the head wreathes...\nROSE: You mean, why you look like a waitress at the House of Pancakes.\nCAROLINE: O.K...What you are wearing on your heads are called Lucia wreaths. We wear them in honor of Lucia, a brave and noble woman I admire very muc…",
      "CAROLINE: Well dig in everyone....don't be shy.\nMARY: Did you eat your hamburger at Hojos?\nCAROLINE: a Mary, try the Lutfish. It's been a À sitting in salt for seven days.\nMARY: Mmmm. ..my favorite.",
      "ROSE: i I'm just trying to understand...\nROSE: We're all family. You argue in front of everyone - why can't we talk\nROSE: in front of everyone?\nCAROLINE: — 7 Because it isn't \"everyone's\" business.",
      "CAROLINE: It's empty - you have to get another bottle.\nROSE: Where are they all going?\nCONNIE: That doctor's cute - I think it's a little strange they're all together here."
